      "info": [
        {
          "id": "f1",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Read the requirements",
          "text": "List every input and required output.\n\nSeparate rules from background detail.\n\nAgree what valid inputs mean.\n\nChallenge: Which inputs and output are required?\n\nThree hour values are inputs. The combined charge is the output."
        },
        {
          "id": "f2",
          "face": "right",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Break down the solution",
          "text": "Separate input, calculation and reporting.\n\nGive each sub-problem a clear purpose.\n\nCombine the results consistently.\n\nChallenge: How could Calculate charges be refined?\n\nCalculate each item charge, add it to the running total and apply any required discount."
        },
        {
          "id": "f3",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Build the running total",
          "text": "Initialise total once before repetition.\n\nRead hours for each item.\n\nAdd hours * 3 to the total.\n\nChallenge: What total results from hours 1, 2 and 3?\n\n3 + 6 + 9 = 18."
        },
        {
          "id": "f4",
          "face": "back",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Apply a rule once",
          "text": "Apply a whole-order discount after summing.\n\nMatch the threshold exactly.\n\nDo not repeatedly discount intermediate totals.\n\nChallenge: What should happen to totals 29 and 30?\n\n29 stays 29. 30 qualifies and becomes 25."
        },
        {
          "id": "f5",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 920,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Selection inside repetition",
          "text": "Decisions can apply to individual items.\n\nKeep per-item rules inside the loop.\n\nKeep whole-order rules after the loop.\n\nChallenge: Where should a per-item long-hire check go?\n\nInside the loop, so every item is checked using its own hours."
        },
        {
          "id": "f6",
          "face": "left",
          "x": 1888,
          "y": 540,
          "title": "Test the complete design",
          "text": "Calculate expected results independently.\n\nTest both sides of a decision boundary.\n\nRecord actual output and compare.\n\nChallenge: Why is the second test useful?\n\nIt reaches the exact discount boundary of 30 and checks that the result is 25."
        }
